{"seq":3,"slug":"ideas-and-methods","title":"理查德·汉明·思想与方法","stage":"DONE","category":"richard-hamming","categoryLabel":"理查德·汉明","chapterCount":3,"docCount":6,"url":"/l-doc-books/c/people/richard-hamming/ideas-and-methods","rating":{"composite":4.06,"verdict":"stable","groups":{"quality":3.6,"coverage":3.5,"positioning":4.67,"strategic":4.67},"weights":{"quality":0.3,"coverage":0.25,"positioning":0.2,"strategic":0.25},"profile":null},"hubDir":"/Users/wangyang.learnwy/learnwy/learnwy/l-doc-hub/hubs/famous-people/06_richard-hamming/3_ideas-and-methods","introHtml":"<h1 id=\"思想与方法\">思想与方法</h1><p>本卷剖析理查德·汉明关于「如何做出伟大科研工作」的方法论。其源头是一份具体文本：1986 年 3 月 7 日他在贝尔通信研究公司（Bellcore）所做、由 J. F. 凯泽录音整理的演讲《你和你的研究》（<a href=\"https://gwern.net/doc/science/1986-hamming\">gwern.net 转录</a>）。本卷不复述原文，而是把汉明散落的论断<strong>结构化为一套相互咬合的杠杆</strong>，并用他生平中的实证（如 1950 年的汉明码）逐条印证。</p>\n<h2 id=\"本卷-vs-兄弟卷的分工\">本卷 vs 兄弟卷的分工</h2><p>汉明的人物条目共六卷，分工明确，避免重复：</p>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>卷</th>\n<th>回答的问题</th>\n<th>与本卷关系</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody><tr>\n<td><a href=\"../life-and-times/\">1 生平与时代</a></td>\n<td>他是谁、经历了什么</td>\n<td>提供方法论的传记背景</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><a href=\"../core-contributions/\">2 核心贡献</a></td>\n<td>他做出了什么（汉明码等）</td>\n<td>本卷用作方法论的「实证案例」</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>3 思想与方法（本卷）</strong></td>\n<td>他<strong>如何</strong>做出伟大工作</td>\n<td>提炼可习得的方法论</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><a href=\"../major-works/\">4 主要著作</a></td>\n<td>成果的载体与影响</td>\n<td>方法论的产物</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><a href=\"../influence-and-legacy/\">5 影响与遗产</a></td>\n<td>他改变了什么</td>\n<td>方法论的长期外溢</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><a href=\"../controversies-and-appraisal/\">6 争议与评价</a></td>\n<td>他的主张有何局限</td>\n<td>对本卷主张的批判性平衡</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<p>一句话：<strong>核心贡献卷讲「做了什么」，本卷讲「为什么能做到」，争议卷讲「这套方法有何边界」。</strong></p>\n<h2 id=\"三章的逻辑链\">三章的逻辑链</h2><p>本卷三章不是并列清单，而是一条因果链：</p>\n<pre class=\"mermaid\" data-diagram-type=\"flowchart\" data-source=\"flowchart LR&#10;    A[&quot;第1章 你和你的研究&lt;br/&gt;演讲背景 + 总纲&quot;] --&gt; B[&quot;第2章 重要问题&lt;br/&gt;选题 + 勇气与远见&quot;]&#10;    B --&gt; C[&quot;第3章 思考的风格&lt;br/&gt;知识复利 + 开门关门&quot;]&#10;    A -.总纲索引.-&gt; B&#10;    A -.总纲索引.-&gt; C\">flowchart LR\n    A[\"第1章 你和你的研究&lt;br/&gt;演讲背景 + 总纲\"] --&gt; B[\"第2章 重要问题&lt;br/&gt;选题 + 勇气与远见\"]\n    B --&gt; C[\"第3章 思考的风格&lt;br/&gt;知识复利 + 开门关门\"]\n    A -.总纲索引.-&gt; B\n    A -.总纲索引.-&gt; C</pre><ul>\n<li><strong>第 1 章·你和你的研究</strong>：<a href=\"you-and-your-research/the-famous-talk\"><code>1_the-famous-talk.md</code></a> 交代史实与文本来源；<a href=\"you-and-your-research/doing-great-work\"><code>2_doing-great-work.md</code></a> 给出五条杠杆的总纲与索引。</li>\n<li><strong>第 2 章·重要问题的选择</strong>：<a href=\"the-importance-of-problems/working-on-important-problems\"><code>1_working-on-important-problems.md</code></a> 讲「重要 × 可攻击」的选题二维判断；<a href=\"the-importance-of-problems/courage-and-vision\"><code>2_courage-and-vision.md</code></a> 讲选题之后的执行品质。</li>\n<li><strong>第 3 章·思考的风格</strong>：<a href=\"style-of-thinking/compound-interest-of-knowledge\"><code>1_compound-interest-of-knowledge.md</code></a> 讲时间维度的复利积累；<a href=\"style-of-thinking/open-door-vs-closed-door\"><code>2_open-door-vs-closed-door.md</code></a> 讲空间维度的开放策略。</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"推荐学习路径与前置\">推荐学习路径与前置</h2><ul>\n<li><strong>前置知识</strong>：建议先读 <a href=\"../core-contributions/error-correcting-codes/hamming-code\">2 核心贡献·汉明码</a>，理解 1947–1950 年纠错码的诞生——本卷几乎每篇都以它作为方法论的活例。</li>\n<li><strong>顺序读法</strong>：按 1 → 2 → 3 章序，沿上面的逻辑链推进；这是首次阅读的推荐路径。</li>\n<li><strong>主题读法</strong>：若只关心选题，直接读第 2 章；若关心日常工作习惯，直接读第 3 章。</li>\n<li><strong>批判性补读</strong>：读完本卷，务必再读 <a href=\"../controversies-and-appraisal/limitations/idealism-vs-reality\">6 争议与评价·理想与现实</a>，了解这套高方差方法论的局限——汉明的建议并非对所有人、所有处境都适用。</li>\n</ul>\n<p>这些思想之所以历久弥新，在于它们把「伟大工作」从天才的神话还原为<strong>部分可控、可习得的行为</strong>——这也是汉明留给后世最实用的遗产。</p>\n","chapters":[{"seq":1,"slug":"you-and-your-research","title":"你和你的研究","docCount":2,"url":"/l-doc-books/c/people/richard-hamming/ideas-and-methods/you-and-your-research","docs":[{"seq":1,"slug":"the-famous-talk","title":"著名的演讲","url":"/l-doc-books/c/people/richard-hamming/ideas-and-methods/you-and-your-research/the-famous-talk"},{"seq":2,"slug":"doing-great-work","title":"做出伟大的工作","url":"/l-doc-books/c/people/richard-hamming/ideas-and-methods/you-and-your-research/doing-great-work"}]},{"seq":2,"slug":"the-importance-of-problems","title":"重要问题的选择","docCount":2,"url":"/l-doc-books/c/people/richard-hamming/ideas-and-methods/the-importance-of-problems","docs":[{"seq":1,"slug":"working-on-important-problems","title":"研究重要的问题","url":"/l-doc-books/c/people/richard-hamming/ideas-and-methods/the-importance-of-problems/working-on-important-problems"},{"seq":2,"slug":"courage-and-vision","title":"勇气与远见","url":"/l-doc-books/c/people/richard-hamming/ideas-and-methods/the-importance-of-problems/courage-and-vision"}]},{"seq":3,"slug":"style-of-thinking","title":"思考的风格","docCount":2,"url":"/l-doc-books/c/people/richard-hamming/ideas-and-methods/style-of-thinking","docs":[{"seq":1,"slug":"compound-interest-of-knowledge","title":"知识的复利","url":"/l-doc-books/c/people/richard-hamming/ideas-and-methods/style-of-thinking/compound-interest-of-knowledge"},{"seq":2,"slug":"open-door-vs-closed-door","title":"开门与关门","url":"/l-doc-books/c/people/richard-hamming/ideas-and-methods/style-of-thinking/open-door-vs-closed-door"}]}]}